<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Aliwal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1846">1846</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Aliwal was fought on 28 January 1846 near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a>. A British force under Sir Harry Smith defeated a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> army under Ranjodh Singh Majithia, driving it back across the river and removing the threat to Ludhiana. It was one of the most complete British victories of the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-aliwal.jpg" alt="Battle of Aliwal" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_d%27Aliwal_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
